<refentry xmlns="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xmlns:svg="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" xmlns:db="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook" version="5.0-subset Scilab" xml:lang="en" xml:id="convex_hull_3"><info><pubdate>29/11/2005</pubdate></info><refnamediv><refname>convex_hull_3</refname><refpurpose>Convex hull in 3d space.</refpurpose></refnamediv>
  
   
  
   
  
   
    
   
  
   
  
   <refsynopsisdiv><title>Calling Sequence</title><synopsis>H=convex_hull_3(x, y, z);</synopsis></refsynopsisdiv>
  
   <refsection><title>Parameters</title>
  
      <variablelist>
    
         <varlistentry>
      
            <term>x, y, z</term>
      
            <listitem>
        : are vectors of points coordinates in 3d space.
      </listitem>
    
         </varlistentry>
    
         <varlistentry>
      
            <term>H</term>
      
            <listitem>
        : is (nbFacets,degreeOfFacet) array of  points indices, each row of H contain one facet of the convex hull of X.
      </listitem>
    
         </varlistentry>
  
      </variablelist>
  
   </refsection>
  
   <refsection><title>Description</title>
    
      <para>
      The function convex_hull_3 computes the convex hull of a given set of three-dimensional points.
    </para>
  
   </refsection>

   <refsection><title>Examples</title><programlisting role="example"><![CDATA[

        x =rand(1,10);
        y =rand(1,10);
        z =rand(1,10);
        H=convex_hull_3(x,y,z);
 
  ]]></programlisting></refsection>
  
